message: "If you use pyweatherfiles in your research, please cite it using the metadata from this file."
title: "pyweatherfiles"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Sánchez-García"
    given-names: "Daniel"
    email: "daniel.sanchezgarcia@uca.es"
    affiliation: "Universidad de Cádiz"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-3080-0821"
abstract: "pyweatherfiles is a Python package for weather-file management aimed at building energy simulation: Typical Meteorological Year (TMY) generation with the Sandia/TMY3 method, conversion between EPW, .met and hourly CSV/Excel series, heating and cooling degree-hours, multi-year climate-trend analysis, EPW file comparison, and cleaning and gap-filling of raw hourly series."
keywords:
  - "Typical Meteorological Year"
  - "TMY"
  - "weather files"
  - "EPW"
  - "building energy simulation"
  - "degree-hours"
  - "climate trends"
  - "Python"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/termotecnia/pyweatherfiles"
url: "https://pyweatherfiles.readthedocs.io/"
doi: "10.5281/zenodo.23310981"
identifiers:
